; Fuzzing (review item R1).
;
; Two laws over every registered target, from a fixed seed:
;
;   - text: random and mutated assembly text goes through the parser, the
;     normalizer, lowering and image planning, and the call returns - a result
;     or diagnostics, never an exception;
;   - bytes: random bytes go through the canonical disassembler, which returns
;     too, and whatever it prints must re-assemble to something that prints the
;     same text again (decode, re-encode, decode is stable).
;
; The default run is bounded to a few seconds so it stays inside @runtest on
; every leg, the emulated 32-bit ones included. RIVET_FUZZ_ITERS scales it,
; RIVET_FUZZ_SEED changes the seed: `make fuzz` runs a longer one.
;
; Native only and outside the three-runtime gate, for test/props' reason.

(executable
 (name test_fuzz)
 (modes exe)
 (libraries
  qcheck-core
  qcheck-core.runner
  driver
  target_intf
  image
  foundation)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:RIVET_MELANGE=false} true)))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (glob_files_rec %{workspace_root}/fixtures/gas-xref/**))
 (action
  (run ./test_fuzz.exe))
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:RIVET_MELANGE=false} true)))
